    sha256: bcaea58ee40a9dca60a21b0f79c525a1f15e95c6b8315d6aaa73f0f53dd5460f
  body: "# Notional income in the JSA and Income Support guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe
    captured chapter calls income not actually received but treated as held notional income, and lists
    several potential bases including deprivation, available-on-application income, unpaid due income
    and third-party arrangements.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA list of possible bases is not a decision
    that any person has notional income. Actual and notional income, relevant disregards, liable-relative
    payments and service-user exceptions require separate examination. Adjacent older programme text and
    the later memo-qualified provision at DMG 28573 must be reconciled before use; no universal programme-duration
    rule is adopted.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 28568, PDF page 134](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=134)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28569, PDF page 134](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=134)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28571, PDF page 135](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=135)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28573, PDF page 135](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=135)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review
    is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring
    time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document,
    individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter
    reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural
    evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch28`: PDF SHA-256 `bcaea58ee40a9dca60a21b0f79c525a1f15e95c6b8315d6aaa73f0f53dd5460f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f7e554c1af4c7d8b915524f441c1680c5bea7429ac8fff9fd18bc0c925f25c31`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/jsais-gross-other-income
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source says to calculate notional income in the same way as actual income while
      applying the normal rules and any appropriate disregard.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch28/0135
      quote: "28571 Calculate notional income in the same way as actual income 1. Any notional income
        of a child or\nyoung person should be added to their actual income. The total should then be taken
        into account using\nnormal rules, including applying any appropriate disregard.\n\n\n        \
        \                                                   1 JSA Regs, reg 105(14); IS (Gen) Regs, reg
        42(7)"
      locator: DMG 28571
  - target: term/jsais-income-deprivation
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Deprivation is expressly one potential basis of notional income, not a synonym for
      every notional-income case.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch28/0134
      quote: "28569 Notional income may be calculated because of\n\n\n1. deprivation of income\n\n\n2.
        income available if applied for (including special rules for personal pensions)\n\n\n3. income
        due but not yet paid\n\n\n4. income for a member of the family paid to a third party\n\n\n5. income
        for a third party made to a member of the family\n\n\n6. a child or young person attending a boarding
        school."
      locator: DMG 28569
